; terrestris.ordinum.udon — scenario-corpus edition
; Pseudo-real: same genre as arch/vivarium/tabularium/
; terrestris.ordinum.udon (the per-phase Charge/Promise floor as data),
; abridged to four phases and recast in 0.9 idiom. Note the quoted
; cross-phase proto-paths in |defeasance :voids — a domain convention the
; path scenarios lean on hard.

|ordinum[terrestris]
  :title Ordinatio Ordinum — the Terrestris phase floor, as instituted data
  :version 0.1.0
  :status draft-until-first-pinned
  :created <2026-07-11>
  :manifold cube-sphere-3d-voxel
  :reportatio .archive/PHASES.md

  ; One ordinum among a planned many in the tabularium. The SCHEMA here
  ; (phase / charge / promise / defeasance / record) is world-kind-agnostic;
  ; only the CONTENT is Earth-lineage. A regula pins `ordinum@version` as
  ; the floor it may extend but never silently undercut.

  |meta[reading-rules]

    A phase declares CHARGES, PROMISES, and DEFEASANCES, plus a RECORD.

    - CHARGE — what the phase must establish; the gating subset of its
      promises. :tag states arrow-kind, never implementation status:
      gate (hard prerequisite we simulate), earth (Earth's pattern kept
      for fidelity), mech (causality known, no simulable mechanism yet),
      emergent (verify, don't build).
    - PROMISE — a defeasible, forward-facing commitment. Its `.class` is
      its kind and classes stack (`.state.regime`): state, regime,
      capability, limit. `:kept-by <nomos>` — absence = an honest GLOSS,
      greppable, never mistaken for a guarantee. `|predicate` — the
      testable condition; a promise with no predicate cannot be marked
      fulfilled at any tier.
    - DEFEASANCE — explicit retirement of a prior promise. Cross-phase
      references are quoted qualified ids ("N.promise-slug").

  |phase[ante-mundane]
    :num 1
    :name Ante-mundane
    :epithet before the world
    :regime analytic
    Cosmic scale; everything prior to the world. Not a process — a
    parameter block (element abundances, orbital configuration, seed).
    |charge[stable-orbit] :tag gate
      Stable orbit in the habitable zone of a viable, protected system.
    |charge[proper-mass] :tag gate
      Proper mass.
    |charge[protective-architecture] :tag mech
      Protective architecture — moon, outer giants, solar-wind shelter.
      The moon cannot be added non-destructively later, so it is declared
      here; declare-causally-materialize-lazily.
    |promises
      |promise[the-constants].state :from stable-orbit
        The constants themselves — orbit, mass, chemistry, seed: the box
        every later computation happens inside.
        |predicate the Phase-1 parameter block is declared and conserved forward.
    |record
      Proportions and totals of elements, base columns, and most conserved
      values.

  |phase[protogenic]
    :num 2
    :name Protogenic
    :epithet the world is now Formed
    :regime analytic
    A sphere orbiting its star, featureless, hot, brooded upon.
    |charge[axial-tilt] :tag gate
      Axial tilt.
    |charge[spin] :tag gate
      Spin — possibly differential layers.
    |charge[smooth-water-surface] :tag earth
      Smooth, water-covered surface.
    |promises
      |promise[formed-sphere].state
        The sphere itself — formed, and orbiting its star.
      |promise[water-covered-surface].state :from smooth-water-surface
        A smooth, water-covered surface.
      |promise[axial-rhythms].regime :kept-by planet :from axial-tilt
        Tilt and spin produce seasons and the day/night cycle, forever.
        |predicate insolation, declination, and hour-angle are correct for date and latitude.
      |promise[coriolis].capability :from spin :unlocks modern-weather
        Spin bequeaths Coriolis — the skeleton of every future wind belt.

  |phase[primordial]
    :num 3
    :name Primordial
    :epithet the world is now Divided
    :regime analytic-relaxation
    Gas, liquid, and solid separate; a sea level; solid ground beneath.
    Light is ambient and highly diffused — day and night exist, but the
    sun is not yet seen.
    |charge[atmosphere-reservoir] :tag gate
      Atmosphere as a real reservoir, pre-oxygen composition.
    |charge[closed-water-cycle] :tag gate
      Water cycle, closed.
    |charge[seeded-asymmetry] :tag gate
      Enough variation, asymmetry, and seeded noise to awaken the Phase-4
      processes.
    |promises
      |promise[sea-level-datum].state
        The sea-level datum every later elevation is read against.
      |promise[diffused-light].regime
        Ambient, highly-diffused light — day and night exist, but the sun
        is not yet seen through the dense sky.
      |promise[closed-water-cycle].regime :from closed-water-cycle
        A closed, conserved water cycle with its energy-gradient channels.
        |predicate global water mass is conserved — nothing pulled from nothing, nothing drained into nothing.
      |promise[seeded-asymmetry].capability :kept-by noise :from seeded-asymmetry :unlocks plate-tectonics
        The seeded asymmetries and fated noise that awaken the Phase-4
        processes; every later phase amplifies them.
        |predicate a deterministic, per-key asymmetry field exists and is stable under re-query.
    |record
      Reservoir partitions; the water cycle settled to steady state.

  |phase[abyssal]
    :num 4
    :name Abyssal
    :epithet the world is now Alive
    :regime incremental-emergent
    :sub-gates expected
    Deep Time. The world itself becomes a highly dynamic system across
    great orders of temporal magnitude.
    |charge[plate-tectonics] :tag mech
      Plate tectonics and the Wegenerian cycle.
    |charge[emergent-land] :tag gate
      Meaningful non-volcanic land above sea level — delivered by uplift,
      never an initial condition.
    |charge[erosion-carving] :tag gate
      Erosion processes carving real landscapes.
    |promises
      |promise[emerged-land].state :from emergent-land
        THE LAND ITSELF — continents, relief, and drainage networks.
        |predicate land rises above sea level, non-volcanic; land-fraction toward the early-Earth target band.
      |promise[erosion-substrate].regime :kept-by erosion-tile :from erosion-carving
        Fluvial erosion continues running as the geological substrate
        beneath every later phase.
        |predicate erosion runs each geological cycle; its eroded bed is what later phases build on.
      |promise[ore-and-soil].state
        Mineral and ore bodies; soil parent material.
    |defeasances
      |defeasance :voids "2.water-covered-surface" :by emergent-land
        Land now rises above the sea; the surface is no longer wholly
        water-covered.
      |defeasance :voids "3.diffused-light" :by plate-tectonics
        Volcanic clearing begins; the sky thins toward the later phases'
        visible cosmos.
    |record
      The deep sedimentary stack; banded-iron formations; the first
      limestones — life writing itself into rock.
